# Data artifacts live under src/data/ but must never be committed (large / regenerable).
# keep the raw water folder, needed
src/data/raw/basins
src/data/raw/crops
src/data/raw/surplus
src/data/raw/weather
src/data/raw/water/USGS_QA_DUMP
src/data/interim/*
src/data/processed/*
src/data/cache/*
src/build/api-keys.toml
!src/data/**/.gitkeep

# EXCEPTION: the annual, cell-aggregated crop/surplus globals + the static grid are TINY (~6MB each)
# -- one row per (cell, YEAR), not (cell, day) like weather. Committing them lets a fresh clone run
# without the multi-GB raw CDL/surplus sources (the crops/surplus builders short-circuit on these).
# (weather_global_*.parquet stays ignored: ~260MB/year, 4.6GB total -> hosted download / re-fetch.)
!src/data/interim/grid_global.parquet
!src/data/interim/crops_global.parquet
!src/data/interim/surplus_global.parquet

# EXCEPTION: the per-site water data + metadata is the ONLY durable copy of IWQIS nitrate
# (not re-fetchable from any API), so it is tracked in git. The 3.1GB raw IWQIS chunks under
# raw/water/ stay ignored (rebuildable, and the parquets supersede them as source of truth).
!src/data/processed/water/
!src/data/processed/water/**

# EXCEPTION: basins are small (~7MB parquets) and slow to re-fetch (NLDI/KMZ for 83 sites), and
# the 552KB D8 direction raster is a runtime asset site_view needs. Track both.
#
# raw/basins is un-ignored by CONTENT, not with a blanket `**`. It used to be `!src/data/raw/basins/**`,
# which was written for the D8 raster alone and then silently swallowed the 388MB / 16k-file NLDI
# polygon cache widget/static/fetch_basins.py writes beneath it. Add new patterns here per artifact
# rather than widening this back to `**`.
!src/data/processed/basins/
!src/data/processed/basins/**
!src/data/raw/basins/
!src/data/raw/basins/*.parquet
# fetch_basins.py's per-COMID NLDI download cache: ~388MB across ~16k JSONs, resumable and
# regenerable (slowly -- the NLDI quota is 800 requests per window). Belt and braces: the narrowed
# exception above already fails to match it, but this says so out loud.
src/data/raw/basins/nldi/

# EXCEPTION: the widget's surplus display assets. meta/surplus_stats.csv (4KB colour-scale min/max,
# read by BOTH the Iowa heatmap and the Voronoi rain-grid cell colouring) + images/iowa_surplus_*.png
# (~32MB statewide heatmap PNGs). Already generated; the gitignored raw pixels can't rebuild them on
# a fresh clone, so track them so the surplus visuals work without the data download.
!src/data/processed/surplus/
!src/data/processed/surplus/**

# EXCEPTION: the basin-containment graph (~4KB). Read at runtime by access.get_basin_graph ->
# src/splits/conflict_graph.py (the LOFO family splitter), so the honest cross-validation would
# FileNotFoundError on a fresh clone without it. Slow to regenerate (needs all 85 basins). Track it.
!src/data/processed/aux/
!src/data/processed/aux/**

# Python / tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/

# Project memory (mirrors sustag/.gitignore)
MEMORY.md
CLAUDE.md

# macOS Finder cruft (must win over the processed/** exceptions above)
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# never commit the zipped weather bundle (it is the Box download)
src/data/interim.zip

.vscode
.claude
MEMORY.md

__pycache__/
*.pyc

cache/

# EXCEPTION to the `cache/` rule directly above, and it has to sit BELOW it -- gitignore takes the
# LAST matching pattern, so placing this beside the other raw/basins exceptions (as it was) let
# `cache/` win and the raster was never actually tracked despite the comment up there saying it was.
# The directory is re-included first because git will not descend into an excluded directory to
# find a re-included file inside it.
!src/data/raw/basins/cache/
src/data/raw/basins/cache/*
!src/data/raw/basins/cache/direction500m.png

# The static widget's shipped data bundle (grid/covariate binaries, ~38MB per rebuild). Generated by
# widget/static/build_bundle.py from src/data, so it is derived twice over -- and it is republished
# to the gh-pages branch, which is where it belongs.
widget/assets/data/

# Training-run boosters. src/models/models/ is the SCRATCH output of src/models/train.py -- one
# ~5.7MB booster per experimental run, and they accumulate (16 of them at the last count). The
# models that actually ship live in deploy/models/ and stay tracked; copy a run there deliberately
# rather than letting every experiment into history.
src/models/models/

# The generated static site. Built by widget/static/export.py, published to the orphan gh-pages
# branch by widget/static/publish.py -- never committed to main (tens of MB per rebuild).
static-site/
site/
